workedExamples.question_text:
This floor plan gives all measurements in millimetres. Find the area of the entire floor, in square metres.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0)--(5,0)--(5,1.5)--(4,1.5)--(4,3)--(0,3)--cycle;
\path (2.5,0) node[below] {$10\,000$} (0,1.5) node[left] {$6000$} (4.5,1.5) node[above] {$2000$} (4,2.25) node[right] {$3000$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

workedExamples.solution_text:
Subtract the missing rectangle from the enclosing rectangle.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,0)--(5,0)--(5,1.5)--(4,1.5)--(4,3)--(0,3)--cycle;
\draw[dashed] (4,3)--(5,3)--(5,1.5);
\path (2.5,0) node[below] {$10\text{ m}$} (0,1.5) node[left] {$6\text{ m}$} (4.5,3) node[above] {$2\text{ m}$} (5,2.25) node[right] {$3\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$\begin{aligned}10\,000\text{ mm}&=10\text{ m}\\6000\text{ mm}&=6\text{ m}\\2000\text{ mm}&=2\text{ m}\\3000\text{ mm}&=3\text{ m}\\A&=10\times6-2\times3\\&=60-6\\&=54\text{ m}^{2}\end{aligned}$

